  "question": {
    "text": "A hoop and a solid cylinder of same mass and radius are made of a permanent magnetic material with their respective axes. But the magnetic moment of hoop is twice of solid cylinder. They are placed in a uniform magnetic field in such a manner that their magnetic moments make a small angle with the field. If the oscillation periods of hoop and cylinder are <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math> respectively, then:",
